-- Parts II–IV carry the essays (imported above): each piece of an essay bearing on a Part
-- is a block of it, the piece's own text selected from its source, so the Part changes exactly when the
-- essay does. Placed 2026-11-17 by reading every essay linearly, sentence by sentence, asking of each
-- how it bears on hyperactive technology, modern metaphysics and technoanarchocommunism (Avik,
-- 2026-11-16: "Metaphysics & technology are near identical for the initiated"): a piece bearing on
-- several Parts is a block of each. Part IV takes only his words and the records of his statements, with
-- their provenance.
-- a carried piece sits under its Part's heading, so its own headings go one level deeper (a line of
-- `#`s then a space, outside a fenced block); every other line is carried as it is
carried-hashes : List Word → Bool
carried-hashes nil = false
carried-hashes (cons x r) = if weq x #35 then carried-hashes r else weq x #32
